RSQLite bundles third-party source code.
Its terms, as far as they are evident from the sources, are:

src/vendor/nanoarrow/ (nanoarrow 0.9.0, nanoarrow.c, nanoarrow.h, nanoarrow.hpp)
  Copyright: The Apache Software Foundation
  License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  The license text is installed as licenses/nanoarrow-LICENSE.txt, and the NOTICE of the project as licenses/nanoarrow-NOTICE.txt:

    Apache Arrow nanoarrow
    Copyright 2023 The Apache Software Foundation

    This product includes software developed at
    The Apache Software Foundation (http://www.apache.org/).

  nanoarrow.h was changed by RSQLite: the line defining NANOARROW_NAMESPACE reads RSQLite instead of RPkg.
  See src/vendor/nanoarrow/README.md in the source package.

src/vendor/sqlite3/ (the SQLite amalgamation) and src/vendor/extensions/ (csv.c, regexp.c, series.c, uuid.c, sqlite3ext.h)
  Public domain: the authors disclaim copyright, and the sources carry the SQLite blessing in place of a legal notice.

src/vendor/extensions/http.c
  Written for RSQLite; its header says "Public domain / CC0 style".

src/vendor/extensions/extension-functions.c (by Liam Healy, from https://www.sqlite.org/contrib)
  The file states no license or copyright terms.

src/vendor/boost/ (a subset of the Boost C++ libraries, from the BH package)
  Copyright: the individual Boost authors, named in each file.
  License: Boost Software License, Version 1.0, as stated in the file headers.
  A header-only library: the license does not require a notice for object code.
